# Review authority, enforced by GitHub rather than by memory.
#
# One rule: every change takes at least one reviewer who did not write it.
#
# There are deliberately NO per-folder owners here. Folders organise the system; tasks
# organise our work. Mapping a directory to a person would turn the architecture into an
# org chart and quietly decide, before anyone has written a line, who gets to learn what.
# A task assignee is not a subsystem owner, and a reviewer is not a permanent authority.
#
# The extra entries below are not ownership. They are surfaces where a change affects
# everyone's work at once, so everyone reviews it.
#
# TODO: replace the placeholders with GitHub handles (numbered, not lettered: nobody is "person A") once the team is added.

# Every change takes a reviewer who did not write it.
*                               @TEAMMATE-1 @TEAMMATE-2 @TEAMMATE-3 @TEAMMATE-4

